editors-in-chief thing).

00:17:03.300 --> 00:17:05.440
<v The Heroine>One of them will win today's task.

00:17:06.100 --> 00:17:10.892
<v The Heroine>A different one might win next week's,
because the tools are genuinely good at

00:17:10.892 --> 00:17:15.562
<v The Heroine>different things — and learning which
one to reach for, for what, is part of

00:17:15.562 --> 00:17:17.200
<v The Heroine>the fluency we're building.

00:17:18.060 --> 00:17:24.257
<v The Heroine>And in every draft, notice the twenty
percent only you can see.Then, if you're

00:17:24.257 --> 00:17:29.591
<v The Heroine>feeling it: take the pop quiz at
SUNNYVAiLE High — ten questions on

00:17:29.591 --> 00:17:35.710
<v The Heroine>today's episode, plus 2 bonus questions
your score banks butterfly clips, and

00:17:35.710 --> 00:17:39.240
<v The Heroine>yes, that will make sense when you get
there.

00:17:40.140 --> 00:17:46.025
<v The Heroine>Turn on K-S-V-L, ninety-nine point nine,
for this week's anthem — don't just

00:17:46.025 --> 00:17:48.700
<v The Heroine>learn from books, learn from hooks.

00:17:49.560 --> 00:17:54.987
<v The Heroine>And if you've got time to wander, the
